From: EC100 Nerves maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: reject missing secure-memory handoff on EC100

The official SPL/TEE must describe its secure memory before U-Boot hands RAM
to Linux. Do not silently boot without a reservation if the handoff is absent.
This system patch is applied only to the EC100 bootloader build.

--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c
@@ -892,5 +892,11 @@
 	/* OP-TEE */
 	mem = param_parse_optee_mem();
+	if (!mem.size) {
+		printf("EC100: missing OP-TEE memory handoff; refusing boot\n");
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+	printf("EC100: OP-TEE reserved 0x%llx + 0x%llx\n",
+	       (u64)mem.base, (u64)mem.size);
 	ret = bidram_reserve(MEM_OPTEE, mem.base, mem.size);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
